museRISC SoC synthesis with all large arrays on SRAM macros (branch soc-sram-synth, 2026-10-16)
=================================================================================================

Recorded on the development tree CantelopePeel/museRISC (fork PR #17 and
its review rounds; PR numbers in this log are the fork's). Base: fork
main b634ffc = this upstream stack plus the CSR VLMAX shift / PLIC tree
(upstream #45), the PLIC spec fixes (#48) and the AES S-box (#35).
Round-3 state of fork PR #17. The branch is rebased onto main edf395e (#26/#27);
every RTL change in b634ffc..edf395e is inside `ifndef SYNTHESIS or a
comment (checked line by line), so the synthesized netlist is unchanged
and synthesis was not re-run; the simulation gates below ran on the
edf395e-based tree.

RTL changes in this branch:
  - muserisc_vrf_bank (VRF) and muserisc_sram_sp (L1 data/tag ways)
    instantiate SRAM macros under MUSERISC_SRAM_FAKERAM45 /
    MUSERISC_SRAM_SKY130 (set only by the ORFS configs), each with a
    read-capture register (macros do not hold read data); simulation
    default unchanged.
  - VRF same-row read+write never reaches a replica (round-3 B2):
    muserisc_vec S3 write combining makes element writes full-word when
    the whole word is known; muserisc_vregfile serves a read colliding
    with a full-word write from the write data (full-word write-first
    bypass, replica not read); a read that would collide with a partial
    write is retried a cycle later by the vector unit (asserted never to
    reach the VRF).
  - core: reset PC without an async-load flop.
ORFS configs read the RTL with -DSYNTHESIS (ORFS also passes -D SYNTHESIS).

Image: openroad/orfs:latest (Yosys 0.68+post, read_slang), run as
--user 3001:3000 through a copy of scripts/openroad_docker.sh with
FLOW_VARIANT for the hierarchical runs.

