== Follow-up to fork PR #17 round 3 (fork PR #28, branch soc-sram-followup, fork main fdb0d48) ==
- muserisc_vec: simulation-only check that S3 write rows never decrease
  within an instruction (the invariant that makes the old-vd
  write-invalidation clauses unreachable). Silent in every gate run.
  Mutations (vector TB, sky130 collision-garbage models): validity flag
  ignored (w_cw_hit = row match) FAIL (7); only the four
  write-invalidation clauses removed PASS (13,232,168 cycles).
- sta_synth.tcl: the summary no longer prints a period-minus-WNS fmax
  (the sky130 header showed 18.80 MHz from the rst_ni recovery path);
  it prints WNS/TNS at the SDC period, the worst core_clock setup path,
  and an "fmax summary" of the three bisected minimum periods. The STA
  logs above were regenerated from the same 1_synth.odb files:
  nangate45 6.19 ns (161.67 MHz); sky130hd 81.37 / 54.29 / 43.52 ns
  (12.29 / 18.42 / 22.98 MHz).
- vendor_model_check.sh: docker runs as the invoking user; only the
  vendor's per-access Reading/Writing displays are stripped; its
  same-address WARNING is kept and counted (fails if non-zero):
  0 warnings, VEC TB PASS x3, 36/36 directed. With colliding reads sent
  to the macro (mutation A) the vendor model prints 136,168 warnings
  but the vector TB still passes, because it returns the new data on a
  collision; the srammacro garbage models are what catch it by value.
